      "text": "🚁 Incredible Rescue! 🚁 \nOn February 11, an ASTAR aircrew from the Yuma Air Branch responded to a downed paraglider south of Glamis, CA. First on scene, AMO EMT and U.S. Border Patrol Agent quickly evaluated the injured 54-year-old male, who suffered a pelvic fracture. With support from ground agent EMTs, the subject was stabilized and transported via backboard to a medivac Reach Helicopter, then airlifted to Palm Springs hospital. Teamwork and rapid response saved a life! #RescueMission",
      "text_resolved": "🚁 Incredible Rescue! 🚁 \nOn February 11, an ASTAR aircrew from the Yuma Air Branch responded to a downed paraglider south of Glamis, CA. First on scene, AMO EMT and U.S. Border Patrol Agent quickly evaluated the injured 54-year-old male, who suffered a pelvic fracture. With support from ground agent EMTs, the subject was stabilized and transported via backboard to a medivac Reach Helicopter, then airlifted to Palm Springs hospital. Teamwork and rapid response saved a life! #RescueMission",
