      "text": "Black Hawk Crew Saves Injured Hiker in Franklin Mountains!\n\nThe @CBPAMORegDirSW El Paso Air Branch answered the call for help from El Paso Police and Fire’s COMSAR team after a hiker fell 150 feet on Mammoth Rock Trail. With ground rescue impossible, a UH-60 Black Hawk aircrew performed a daring 250-foot hoist, extracting the injured hiker and rescuers from rugged terrain. The patient was swiftly flown to a Level I trauma center for urgent care. #RescueMission #BlackHawk",
